<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Iltutmish</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">seized throne 1211</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Iltutmish was a Turkic slave commander who seized the throne of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> in 1211. He consolidated the sultanate and in 1229 was recognised by the Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hindustan">Hindustan</a>. He is regarded as the real consolidator of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/iltutmish.jpg" alt="Iltutmish" width="320" height="159" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Islamic_Sultanates._Delhi._Shams_al-D%C4%ABn_Iltutmish._AH_607-633_AD_1210-1235._AR_Tanka_(25mm,_11.07_g,_6h)._Sind_type.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
